{"name":"Green Room","hex":"#80aea4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"green room","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["In a television studio, theatre or concert hall, the room where performers await their entrance.","The inside of a tube (a cylindrical wave)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/green_room"}],"entries":[{"title":"Green room","blocks":[{"text":"In show business, the green room is the space in a theatre, or a similar venue, that functions as a waiting room and lounge for performers before, during, and after a performance or show when they are not engaged on stage. Green rooms typically have seating for the performers, such as upholstered chairs and sofas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Teatro_Real_%28Madrid%29_05.jpg/330px-Teatro_Real_%28Madrid%29_05.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green_room","wikidata":"Q1544656"},{"title":"Green Room (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Green Room is a 2015 American Action horror thriller film written and directed by Jeremy Saulnier, and produced by Neil Kopp, Victor Moyers and Anish Savjani. Starring Anton Yelchin, Imogen Poots, Alia Shawkat, Joe Cole, Callum Turner and Patrick Stewart, the film focuses on a punk band who find themselves attacked by neo-Nazi skinheads after witnessing a murder at a remote club in the Pacific Northwest."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e5/Green_Room_%28film%29_POSTER.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green_Room_(film)","wikidata":"Q18392433"},{"title":"Room","blocks":[{"text":"In a building or a ship, a room is any enclosed space within a structure, typically bounded by walls to which entry is possible only via a door or other dividing structure. The entrance connects it to either a passageway, another room, or the outdoors. The space is typically large enough for several people to move about. The size, fixtures, furnishings, and sometimes placement of the room within the building or ship support the activity to be conducted in it."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Ateneul_Rom%C3%A2n_-_Sala.jpg/330px-Ateneul_Rom%C3%A2n_-_Sala.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Room","wikidata":"Q180516"},{"title":"Green","blocks":[{"text":"Green is the color between cyan and yellow on the visible spectrum. It has 295–350 different shades. It is evoked by light which has a dominant wavelength of roughly 495–570 nm. In subtractive color systems, used in painting and color printing, it is created by a combination of yellow and cyan; in the RGB color model, used on television and computer screens, it is one of the additive primary colors, along with red and blue, which are mixed in different combinations to create all other colors. By far the largest contributor to green in nature is chlorophyll, the chemical by which plants photosynthesize and convert sunlight into chemical energy. Many creatures have adapted to their green environments by taking on a green hue themselves as camouflage. Several minerals have a green color, including the emerald, which is colored green by its chromium content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg/330px-Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green","wikidata":"Q3133"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Green_Room_at_the_Traverse_Theatre%2C_Edinburgh_Doors_Open_Day_2007_%281464973302%29.jpg/500px-Green_Room_at_the_Traverse_Theatre%2C_Edinburgh_Doors_Open_Day_2007_%281464973302%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Green_Room_at_the_Traverse_Theatre%2C_Edinburgh_Doors_Open_Day_2007_%281464973302%29.jpg/500px-Green_Room_at_the_Traverse_Theatre%2C_Edinburgh_Doors_Open_Day_2007_%281464973302%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The green room at the Traverse Theatre, Edinburgh","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGreen_Room_at_the_Traverse_Theatre%2C_Edinburgh_Doors_Open_Day_2007_(1464973302).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e2/Green_Room_Soundtrack.jpg/250px-Green_Room_Soundtrack.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e2/Green_Room_Soundtrack.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e2/Green_Room_Soundtrack.jpg/250px-Green_Room_Soundtrack.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGreen_Room_Soundtrack.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Anton_Yelchin_TIFF_2015.jpg/500px-Anton_Yelchin_TIFF_2015.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Anton_Yelchin_TIFF_2015.jpg/1280px-Anton_Yelchin_TIFF_2015.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Anton_Yelchin_TIFF_2015.jpg/500px-Anton_Yelchin_TIFF_2015.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Actor Anton Yelchin at the 2015 Toronto International Film Festival premiere of Green Room. It was his last feature film released while he was alive.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnton_Yelchin_TIFF_2015.